---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const SWATCHES = [
  { name: "Sky", hex: "#A8C7DC", cls: "bg-sky", role: "Cool relief, section grounds" },
  { name: "Off-white", hex: "#FFF8F0", cls: "bg-offwhite", role: "Default page ground" },
  { name: "Cream", hex: "#F8E9C8", cls: "bg-cream", role: "Warm secondary ground" },
  { name: "Ink", hex: "#221F18", cls: "bg-ink", role: "Primary text, dark grounds" },
  { name: "Deep green", hex: "#2B3B2E", cls: "bg-green", role: "Dark ground, secondary brand" },
  { name: "Maroon", hex: "#5C2020", cls: "bg-maroon", role: "The wordmark colour. Primary brand." },
  { name: "Terracotta", hex: "#8C4227", cls: "bg-terracotta", role: "Warm accent. Light grounds only." },
];

/* Measured with the WCAG 2.1 relative-luminance formula against the exact
   values extracted from color-palette.jpeg. */
const CONTRAST = [
  ["Ink", "Off-white", "15.61", "AAA"],
  ["Ink", "Cream", "13.69", "AAA"],
  ["Ink", "Sky", "9.29", "AAA"],
  ["Maroon", "Off-white", "11.85", "AAA"],
  ["Maroon", "Cream", "10.39", "AAA"],
  ["Maroon", "Sky", "7.05", "AAA"],
  ["Green", "Off-white", "11.28", "AAA"],
  ["Green", "Cream", "9.89", "AAA"],
  ["Green", "Sky", "6.71", "AA"],
  ["Terracotta", "Off-white", "6.82", "AA"],
  ["Terracotta", "Cream", "5.98", "AA"],
  ["Terracotta", "Ink", "2.29", "Fail"],
  ["Terracotta", "Green", "1.65", "Fail"],
];

const TONES = ["sky", "cream", "terracotta", "maroon", "green", "ink"];
---

<Base
  title="Design system — OLMIKAYA"
  description="The OLMIKAYA design system: palette, measured contrast, type scale and components."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="col-7 stack reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">Design system</p>
          <h1 class="display-l">The rules, written down.</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            Everything the site is built from, in one place, so it survives the
            next person who touches it. Values here are extracted from the
            supplied brand assets, not chosen.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2 class="h2">Palette</h2>
        <p class="small muted">Extracted from color-palette.jpeg</p>
      </div>

      <p class="lead measure reveal hang">
        Each swatch in the source file is a uniform block, so these are exact
        source values rather than approximations.
      </p>

      <div class="row row--4 hang">
        {
          SWATCHES.map((s) => (
            <div class="swatch reveal">
              <div class={`swatch__chip ${s.cls}`} />
              <div class="swatch__meta">
                <p class="h3">{s.name}</p>
                <p class="swatch__hex">{s.hex}</p>
                <p class="small muted">{s.role}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section ground-cream">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2 class="h2">Measured contrast</h2>
        <p class="small muted">WCAG 2.1</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid">
        <div class="col-5 stack reveal">
          <p class="statement">
            The palette is unusually well behaved. Nearly every text pairing
            clears AAA, which is what lets the site carry long-form reading
            without compromise.
          </p>
          <p class="note">
            <strong>One binding rule.</strong> Terracotta is a light-ground accent
            only. It must never be used as text or a meaningful mark on ink or
            green. On dark grounds use cream, off-white or sky.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="col-6 start-7 reveal">
          <div class="scroll-x">
            <table class="table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Foreground</th>
                  <th scope="col">Ground</th>
                  <th scope="col">Ratio</th>
                  <th scope="col">Body text</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {
                  CONTRAST.map(([fg, bg, ratio, verdict]) => (
                    <tr>
                      <td>{fg}</td>
                      <td>{bg}</td>
                      <td>{ratio}</td>
                      <td class={verdict === "Fail" ? "fail" : "pass"}>{verdict}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))
                }
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2 class="h2">Typography</h2>
        <p class="small muted">Ovo and Inter</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid">
        <div class="col-5 stack reveal">
          <p class="statement">
            Ovo ships exactly one style: weight 400, no bold, no italic.
          </p>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>
              That single fact shapes the whole system. Ovo is a display face
              only — hierarchy comes from size, letterspacing, case and colour,
              never from weight. Putting a bold or italic tag inside Ovo-set text
              would make the browser synthesise a weight the typeface does not
              have, which reads as broken at editorial scale, so Ovo is scoped to
              headings, the wordmark and pull-quotes.
            </p>
            <p>
              Inter carries everything you actually read: body copy, captions,
              metadata, navigation and UI. It has a real weight range and a true
              italic.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        {/* The whole ladder, in order. It showed six of ten steps before, and
            the four it left out are exactly where the scale fragmented: sizes
            with nowhere to be checked drift. Every step is rendered by the
            house class that carries it — no font-size is declared here. */}
        <div class="col-6 start-7 stack-lg reveal">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">--step-hero &middot; 44–96 &middot; Ovo</p>
            <p class="display-xl">Intentional</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">--step-title &middot; 34–60 &middot; Ovo</p>
            <p class="display-l">Ordinary living</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">--step-feature &middot; 28–48 &middot; Ovo</p>
            <p class="lead-block__title">The long table</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">--step-section &middot; 24–40 &middot; Ovo</p>
            <p class="h2">What we publish</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">--step-sub &middot; 22–32 &middot; Ovo</p>
            <p class="statement">A subhead, a pull-quote, a menu link.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">--step-card &middot; 19–24 &middot; Ovo</p>
            <p class="h3">Salt, and the keeping of it</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">--step-lead &middot; 18–22 &middot; Inter 400</p>
            <p class="lead measure">
              The entry into a piece, set one size above the column it opens.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">--step-body &middot; 17 &middot; Inter 400</p>
            <p class="measure">
              The table is not remarkable. It is three tables, actually, pushed
              end to end and covered with a cloth that does not quite reach the
              corners.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">--step-small &middot; 14 &middot; Inter 400</p>
            <p class="small muted">
              Photograph to come &middot; Nairobi, March 2026
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">--step-label &middot; 12 &middot; Inter 500</p>
            <p class="eyebrow">Food &middot; Ritual</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section ground-sky">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2 class="h2">Plates</h2>
        <p class="small muted">Placeholder imagery</p>
      </div>

      <p class="lead measure reveal">
        Every plate stands in for a photograph, holding the correct aspect ratio
        and a palette colour field. Add a photograph in the CMS and it takes the
        same slot — nothing around it changes.
      </p>

      <div class="row row--4 hang">
        {
          TONES.map((tone) => (
            <div class="stack-sm reveal">
              <div class={`plate plate--square plate--${tone}`} />
              <p class="small muted">
                {tone.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + tone.slice(1)}
              </p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2 class="h2">Components</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="row row--2">
        <div class="stack reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">Pull-quote</p>
          <blockquote class="pullquote">
            Nobody was invited, so nobody can be uninvited.
            <span class="pullquote__attr">A regular, on the rules</span>
          </blockquote>
        </div>

        <div class="stack reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">Directory entry</p>
          <div class="entry">
            <p class="entry__no">001</p>
            <div class="stack-sm">
              <h3 class="entry__name">A roastery in a garage</h3>
              <p class="card__dek">Single origin, one bag at a time.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="entry__place">Nairobi</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="stack reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">Buttons and links</p>
          <div class="subscribe__form">
            <a class="button" href="/journal/">Primary</a>
            <a class="button button--ghost" href="/journal/">Ghost</a>
          </div>
          <a class="more" href="/journal/">Inline more link</a>
        </div>

        <div class="stack reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">Scaffold note</p>
          <p class="note">
            <strong>Scaffold.</strong> Used anywhere a surface is structure rather
            than finished content, so placeholder work can never be mistaken for
            the real thing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section ground-green on-dark">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="col-4 stack reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">Motion</p>
          <h2 class="h2">Almost none</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="col-7 start-6 stack reveal">
          <p class="lead">
            Elements fade and rise a few pixels once, on entry. There is no
            parallax and nothing moves on its own.
          </p>
          <p class="small">
            The hidden state is scoped to a class the script adds, so with
            JavaScript disabled nothing is ever stranded invisible. Readers who
            ask for reduced motion get the finished state immediately, with
            transitions and the scroll observer both switched off.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
